\DOC ENSURES_PRESERVED_TAC

\TYPE {ENSURES_PRESERVED_TAC : string -> term -> tactic}

\SYNOPSIS
Strengthens an {ensures} goal by conjoining to both pre- and postcondition the
claim that the state component {ctm} reads as a fresh variable {pname}, and
adding a {MAYCHANGE} clause for {ctm} to the frame.

\DESCRIBE
{pname : string} names the new variable standing for the component's initial
value, which appears in the added conjuncts; {ctm : term} is the state
component (a readable state field, or a composition of such) whose preservation
is asserted and which is appended to the {MAYCHANGE} frame. Applied to an
{ensures} goal it yields one subgoal, with assumptions unchanged:
{
   A ?- ensures ... P Q R
   =============================== ENSURES_PRESERVED_TAC pname ctm
   A ?- ensures ... P' Q' R'
}
\noindent where {P'} is {P} with {read ctm s = pname} conjoined at the end,
{Q'} is {Q} with the same conjunct added at the end, and {R'} is {R} with
{MAYCHANGE [ctm]} appended as a further {,,} component. In the process the
{,,}-composed frame and the pre/postcondition conjunctions are
re-associated/flattened, so bracketed subgroups of {MAYCHANGE} clauses and of
precondition conjuncts come out as a flat right-nested chain.

\COMMENTS
In all observed traces only this single kind of transformation occurs, always
on {ensures} goals for machine-code programs.

\ENDDOC
